<section class="www-section" id="runtime">
  <header class="www-section-head">
    <div>
      <p class="hara-v2-kicker">03 · Runtime model</p>
      <h2>The host changes without replacing the language.</h2>
    </div>
    <p>
      Begin with a browser session, work inside the JVM ecosystem, or use the native Rust runtime. Each mode states its engine, deployment boundary, and intended use.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="www-runtime-workbench">
    <div class="www-runtime-workbench__rail">
      <span>Kernel mode</span>
      <div class="www-runtime-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Kernel mode">
        <button type="button" role="tab" id="kernel-tab-java" data-kernel-tab="java" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="kernel-panel-java" tabindex="0"><strong>Java</strong><small>JVM / Truffle</small></button>
        <button type="button" role="tab" id="kernel-tab-native" data-kernel-tab="native" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="kernel-panel-native" tabindex="-1"><strong>Native</strong><small>Rust / Whole-Wasm</small></button>
        <button type="button" role="tab" id="kernel-tab-web" data-kernel-tab="web" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="kernel-panel-web" tabindex="-1"><strong>Web</strong><small>Browser / WASM</small></button>
      </div>
      <p>Arrow keys move between modes. Home and End select the first and last mode.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="www-runtime-panel" id="kernel-panel-java" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="kernel-tab-java" data-kernel-mode="java">
      <header><code>Java</code><span class="hara-v2-badge">JVM host</span></header>
      <h3>Work inside the JVM ecosystem.</h3>
      <p>Run with the Truffle runtime, integrate with Java classes and tools, and target Native Image when a self-contained deployment is useful.</p>
      <dl><div><dt>Engine</dt><dd>Truffle AST / HBC4</dd></div><div><dt>Deployment</dt><dd>JVM or Native Image</dd></div><div><dt>Best for</dt><dd>Java systems and language tooling</dd></div></dl>
    </div>
    <div class="www-runtime-panel" id="kernel-panel-native" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="kernel-tab-native" data-kernel-mode="native" hidden>
      <header><code>Native</code><span class="hara-v2-badge" data-tone="signal">Primary runtime</span></header>
      <h3>Use the high-performance Rust runtime.</h3>
      <p><b>hara-rust-full</b> prepares whole-function WebAssembly and hosts it natively for tools, services, local applications, and embedded products.</p>
      <dl><div><dt>Engine</dt><dd>Whole-Wasm</dd></div><div><dt>Deployment</dt><dd>Native binary or library</dd></div><div><dt>Best for</dt><dd>Services, CLIs, and embedded products</dd></div></dl>
    </div>
    <div class="www-runtime-panel" id="kernel-panel-web" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="kernel-tab-web" data-kernel-mode="web" hidden>
      <header><code>Web</code><span class="hara-v2-badge" data-tone="success">Available here</span></header>
      <h3>Run a real Hara kernel in the browser.</h3>
      <p>Start with the interpreter core, then load VM, trace, or whole-Wasm compilation capabilities only when the application needs them.</p>
      <dl><div><dt>Small</dt><dd>Interpreter core</dd></div><div><dt>Full</dt><dd>VM + whole-Wasm compiler</dd></div><div><dt>Best for</dt><dd>Learning, tools, and browser applications</dd></div></dl>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="www-section-action"><a href="/benchmarks/">Compare runtime artifacts and methods →</a></div>
</section>
